8. Push Function
Question: Store all salaries of each city in an array.
db.col.aggregate([
  {
    $group:{
      _id:"$City",
      cityCount:{$push:"$Salary"}
    }
  }
])

Output
{ "_id" : "Thane",  "cityCount" : [ 60000 ] }
{ "_id" : "Mumbai", "cityCount" : [ 12000, 3000, 83000 ] }
{ "_id" : "Pune",   "cityCount" : [ 55000 ] }

$push keeps duplicate values if they exist. The journal demonstrates this array-collection operation.     BDNS Journal
9. addToSet Function
Question: Store unique salaries of each city.
db.col.aggregate([
  {
    $group:{
      _id:"$City",
      cityCount:{$addToSet:"$Salary"}
    }
  }
])

Output
{ "_id" : "Thane",  "cityCount" : [ 60000 ] }
{ "_id" : "Mumbai", "cityCount" : [ 12000, 3000, 83000 ] }
{ "_id" : "Pune",   "cityCount" : [ 55000 ] }

The difference is:
$push      → adds values to an array
$addToSet  → adds only unique values

The journal includes both operations.     BDNS Journal
